spans.s:
फ॑ल n. (adj. —˚ f. आ & ई) fruit, esp. of a tree,
kernel, testicle;
 fruit i.e. result, profit, gain, reward or punishment,
compensation, interest on capital;
 tablet, board, blade, point of an
arrow. f. आ & ई names of plants.

फा॑ल m. (*n.) ploughshare or a kind of shovel;
 bundle,
bunch, nosegay.

फलक (adj. —˚ f. ˚लिका) result, advantage.* gain;
abstr. ˚त्व n. — फ॑लक n. tablet, board etc. = फ॑ल + a
wooden bench, the palm of the hands, shield.

फलभाग m. share in any product, advantage, or
reward;
 poss. ˚गिन्.

फलिग॑ m. receptacle for water;
 barrel, cask, etc., fig.
a cloud.

फलित a. fruitful, having yielded fruits or
consequences, resulted, fulfilled;
 n. also impers.

फलीक॑रण n. abstr. to prec.;
 m. pl. the refuse
from the cleaned grain.

फलोदय m. the appearance of consequences;
 reward or
punishment for (loc. or —˚).

फल्गु॑ (f. फल्गु॑, फ˚ल्गू॑ & फ˚ल्ग्वी) reddish;
 small,
minute, weak (abstr. ˚ता† f.);
 f. du. N. of a lunar mansion.

फ॑ल्गुन a. reddish, red. m. E. of Arjuna;
 f. ई sgl. &
du. N. of a double lunar mansion.

फा॑लकृष्ट a. tilled with the plough, s. ploughed
land;
 growing on tilled ground, m. such fruit.
